  "articleBody": "When you're looking to refresh your interior trim, picking the right paint isn't just about color; it's about durability and how it holds up to daily life. You've probably got questions like what kind of prep is included, whether the trim will be sanded, how many coats are standard, and what exact paint product and finish will be used, right? These are all super valid. For high-traffic areas, you’ll want a durable finish that can stand up to bumps and scuffs. Ask your painter for a written scope that details exactly which trim areas are included, the brand and type of paint (like a specific Behr product, for example) and the finish, and if things like caulk repairs are part of the deal. Also, confirm how many coats they plan to apply and whether they'll handle moving furniture and protecting your nearby surfaces. A good painter will be upfront about all this! If you have lots of detailed trim work, or if your current trim has old oil-based finishes that need special treatment for a new waterborne paint, a professional can really make a difference. We serve the entire Denver metro area, from Aurora to Boulder and beyond, and we can help you get these details sorted for a beautiful, lasting finish.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
